      "name": "a comparison orders strings by Unicode code point too",
      "why": "The astral hazard is not confined to bucket keys: `>` and `<` go through the same string ordering. U+1F600 (😀) is a surrogate pair, so a TypeScript `>` reads it as BELOW U+FF01 (！) and this filter would return nothing. Code-point order — what Rust's UTF-8 byte comparison already is — puts it above.",
