    {
      "name": "a string literal coerces to a number against a numeric field",
      "why": "Kinds reconcile toward the OBSERVED value, so `\"2.0\"` compares numerically against a stored 2 and matches — where a string comparison of `2` against `2.0` would not. This is also what pins the shared number rendering: an integral value renders without a fractional part on both hosts.",
